 "path": ".openclaw/tmp/continual_arc_rectangular_outline.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC pattern note: complete rectangle perimeter

For this puzzle family, a single non-background marker color forms scattered fragments of the perimeter of its axis-aligned bounding rectangle. Find min/max row and column containing markers. Along all four edges of that bounding box, preserve existing marker cells and replace missing/background edge cells with color 2. Leave all cells strictly inside and outside the bounding box unchanged. Do not fill the rectangle interior.

Evidence from solved task-aee3875c: marker color 5, background 7; bounds rows 3..23, columns 1..24. The correct output changed missing cells on top/bottom and left/right edges to 2, including bottom-row gaps and missing side cells, while leaving the interior 7s untouched. Demonstrations with marker colors 3 and 0 showed the same perimeter-completion rule using 2, preserving original markers."
}
